WEBVTT

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:05.230
Once spring break's over, 
we'll be third-years.

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:08.190
It doesn't feel like anything's changed.

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:09.480
I know, right?

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.640
Entrance exams... I don't wanna!

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:18.260
By the way, all of you already know 
what you want to do next... right?

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:20.080
Yeah, pretty much.

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:22.110
Yes, I suppose.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:23.080
Me, too!

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.050
Yeah...

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.080
What's wrong?

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:31.090
It's probably not great if I haven't 
decided on anything by now, huh?

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:38.240
Both of my parents are fine 
with wherever I want to go...

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:42.100
m 0 0 l 100 0 l 100 56 l 0 56

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:42.100
Ichika's Mother
Yuriko

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.660
But I don't have anything in 
particular that I want to pursue.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:46.060
Well, I don't think you 
need to decide in a hurry.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:49.980
Hey, to give me some ideas, could you 
all tell me what you plan to do?

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:51.610
Sure!

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:53.560
I guess I'll go first.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:56.340
I want to be a PE teacher, so I plan to get

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.820
my teaching license at a public university.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:03.510
You've wanted to be a PE teacher 
ever since you were in first grade.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:04.710
Yeah, exactly.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:09.160
I considered a private school, 
but I don't think we can afford it.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:14.260
I'd probably have to get a student loan, 
so I'd need a part-time job!

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:15.650
I see.

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:16.590
And you, Ruri?

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:19.760
I'll be going to a fashion design school.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:25.370
Once I graduate, I'm hoping I'll 
be able to make my own brand

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:26.870
and sell things online.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:28.560
Wow, that's great!

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.000
That's awesome.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.100
Sweet!

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:32.820
Thanks.

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:36.400
But my mother's against the idea.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:37.230
Huh?

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:42.830
But I plan to do this and that to try and 
convince her otherwise, so it'll be fine.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:44.790
<b>This
and
that...</b>

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:44.790
All right. You're next, Rio.

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:49.040
Well... I want to be a lawyer.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:50.790
What? I didn't know that!

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:53.770
Yeah, because I haven't told anyone 
but my family and teachers.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:57.510
Is there a reason you 
want to become a lawyer?

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.440
I mean, lawyers are awesome.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.510
<b>Boom</b>

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:03.170
Your reasoning is awesome!

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:07.460
So, yeah. I'm trying to get into 
a school that teaches law.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:11.190
It's gonna be a lot of work, 
but I want to do everything I can.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:14.420
That's so amazing. Way to go, Rio.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:16.790
Do your parents support you in this decision?

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:19.940
Well, they aren't against it, 
so I'm going to assume they are.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:22.860
My dad's always been pretty easy on me.

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:28.940
What was it like when Ryo-san 
decided what he wanted to do?

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:29.850
My brother?

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:31.500
Hey, I wanna know, too!

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.790
That might help us out in some way.

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.800
Hmm... I don't really remember.

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:40.110
We're talking about when I was about seven,

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:43.210
and I wasn't that interested, 
so I never asked.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:47.390
Ryo-san graduated from a pretty 
good school, didn't he?

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:47.950
Yeah.

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:50.250
Oh, I knew it.

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:53.520
I have no idea what he studied at school.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.380
Maybe he learned how to 
mess around with girls.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:58.780
<b>Du-dun</b>

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:58.780
Come on, now...

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.760
<b>A
ha
ha</b>

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.340
I'm just kidding.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:03.660
<i>I think she was half serious, though.</i>

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:08.540
You're all so ahead of the game. 
I guess I need to think about this, too.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:13.210
Then why not try to decide 
based on what you like to do?

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.250
Hey, that's a great idea!

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:20.770
What I like to do, huh?

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:52.020
Koikimo

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:57.020
Episode 11

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:57.020
"High Schooler"

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:03.240
I thought about giving you this 
once the new school year started,

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:06.400
but I really didn't want to wait two weeks.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:08.590
It's for White Day.

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:10.700
Oh, thank you so much!

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:14.410
I mean... it was just the right thing 
to do, since you gave me something.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:19.210
By the way, when I was hanging out 
with Rio and the others yesterday,

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:21.550
we were talking about what we plan to do next.

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:23.410
Are you going to college?

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:24.160
Yeah.

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:29.050
For now, I'm hoping to get 
into a liberal arts school.

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:32.460
Oh! Me, too... I think.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:34.300
What? You're not sure?

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:37.630
I'm wondering if I'm 
actually serious about it.

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:43.690
I'm hoping I'll find out what I 
want to do once I get into college.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:47.180
I see. I guess that's an option, too.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:51.400
You're so earnest, Arima. I think it's 
fine if you're not completely sure yet.

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:54.220
Yeah, but...

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:59.460
I think I'm panicking a little because 
I can't picture what I want to do.

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:06.300
But you were a lot of help. Thank you.

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:08.780
Why not try asking people older than us, too?

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:09.890
Huh?

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:13.840
They've already been through all this,

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:15.720
so I bet they could give you good advice.

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:18.270
Someone older...

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:26.300
<i>I think it'd be a good idea to 
start with something you like.</i>

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:26.740
Ryo-san

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:29.270
<i>You like art, don't you?</i>

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:30.490
Yes.

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:33.190
Then what about an art school?

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:35.890
<i>Huh? No, that's impossible.</i>

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:39.540
I like to draw and paint, but I'm 
not particularly good at either.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:39.540
I suck at
sketching

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:44.130
<i>And if I had to choose, I think I like 
looking at art more than making it.</i>

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:45.550
I see.

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:48.580
Does that mean you might be 
interested in a job where you can

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:50.430
observe and study art pieces?

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:52.670
<i>Maybe like a curator.</i>

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:56.900
Oh, I see. I guess there 
are jobs like that, too.

00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:59.810
<i>A curator, huh?</i>

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:02.970
<i>How did you decide which school to go to?</i>

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:05.440
Me? I...

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:10.540
You can't even think for yourself. 
Don't you dare try to defy your parents.

00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:16.320
I just followed the path that 
my parents laid out for me.

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:17.200
<i>Huh?</i>

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:20.250
<i>So you shouldn't use me as an example.</i>

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:20.960
Ryo-san

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.300
<i>Oh, I'm sure Masuda would be 
much more helpful with this.</i>

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:27.830
<i>He actually went to an art school.</i>

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:30.100
I'll ask him next time I see him.

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:32.680
<i>Thank you very much.</i>

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:35.320
It's a bit late tonight, so I'll let you go.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:36.510
<i>Oh, sure.</i>

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:38.280
<i>Goodnight, Ichika-san.</i>

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:40.230
Goodnight.

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:48.570
<i>Maybe I'll go to</i>

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:52.140
<i>the library tomorrow to get some 
books on certifications and stuff...</i>

00:07:56.700 --> 00:08:00.660
<b>Introduction
to Curatorship</b>

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.410
<b>How to Explore Art Museums</b>

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.410
<b>Introduction
to Curatorship</b>

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.170
<b>An Art Gallery for the New Century</b>

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:08.500
<b>An Art Gallery for the New Century</b>

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:18.510
It's been so long since the 
four of us ate as a family.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:20.980
Yeah, you're right.

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:23.570
Sorry I'm rarely home.

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:27.050
It's okay. Onii-chan helps me out a lot.

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:31.110
I see. Oh, Rio, could you pass the dressing?

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:32.650
Here.

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:33.660
Thanks.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:39.410
Ryo.

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:42.060
Are you staying here tonight?

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:44.540
No. I'm going back to my apartment.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:46.540
I see.

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:57.430
Those two haven't changed at all.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:59.240
Are we living
in the Ice Age?

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:58.760
Yeah...

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:00.100
Mom.

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.720
I can clean up for you.

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:05.510
You must be tired from your business trip.

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:06.850
Oh, it's fine.

00:09:07.090 --> 00:09:09.090
Let me do this every once in a while.

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:11.750
Do you even remember how 
to use the dishwasher?

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:13.040
I'll ask Rio.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:14.650
Figures.

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:17.280
Okay, sure. Thanks.

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:24.080
So, how are Ryo and Ichika-chan doing lately?

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:28.900
Hmm... I guess there's been at least 
some progress since they first met.

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:31.030
What kind of progress?

00:09:31.930 --> 00:09:36.100
She gave him a Valentine's Day gift, 
and they went out on a date for White Day.

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:39.090
Are you really talking about Ryo?

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:42.390
This all sounds so pure that it's scaring me.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:44.100
Sure it's not
just someone
with the
same name?

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:44.100
Yeah, I feel you.

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:47.040
It is a bit surprising if you think about it.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:50.030
I was shocked when you told me.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:51.860
Right?

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:55.490
Who would've thought Onii-chan would 
develop a crush on one of my friends?

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:56.290
Rio.

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:00.540
What do you mean by that?

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.320
Ryo, hang on a second.

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:10.610
What?

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:14.150
You had the nerve to lay your 
hands on one of Rio's friends?

00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:16.820
She's still in high school!

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:17.630
What?

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:19.470
Lay my hands on her?

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:21.260
Why do you have to say it like that?

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:23.310
So it's true.

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:26.930
How are you so lacking in common sense?

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:30.750
If you could hold yourself 
responsible for whatever happens

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:32.890
in your work or private life, it'd be fine.

00:10:32.890 --> 00:10:36.320
But it's a different story if you're 
dragging Rio down with you.

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:41.250
You're an adult now! 
You need to settle down already!

00:10:41.710 --> 00:10:43.330
Hang on a second.

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:46.810
You didn't even ask me what's going on. 
You just made your own assumptions.

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:49.240
Even if there was a chance of trouble,

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:51.690
I have absolutely no intention 
of dragging Rio into this!

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:52.590
Most importantly...

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:58.140
Ichika-san is one of Rio's closest friends,

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:01.420
so don't ever say it like that to Rio!

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:05.390
You dare speak to your own father that way?!

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:11.400
<i>I'm sorry, Onii-chan.</i>

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:17.150
<i>He just happened to overhear Mom 
and me talking about Ichika...</i>

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:19.740
You have nothing to apologize for.

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:21.850
There's nothing to hide, anyway.

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:23.870
<i>Yeah, I know, but...</i>

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:27.580
<i>He was eavesdropping on 
your conversation, right?</i>

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:31.440
<i>God, he's awful.</i>

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:35.400
<i>You were talking with Dad when 
you were leaving, weren't you?</i>

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:38.640
You don't need to worry about any of that.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:39.630
<i>I guess...</i>

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:44.060
<i>You always get so meek all of a 
sudden when Dad gets involved.</i>

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:45.640
Well...

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:51.610
You two are always so harsh with each other.

00:11:52.780 --> 00:11:53.900
It's scary.

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:57.300
Considering everything I've done so far,

00:11:57.890 --> 00:12:01.080
it's not surprising that Dad 
would have that attitude.

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:03.760
Hey.

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:04.530
<i>Hmm?</i>

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:08.950
<i>What should I say to Dad if 
he asks about you and Ichika?</i>

00:12:14.430 --> 00:12:16.830
Just tell him what you know.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:19.010
There's nothing to hide.

00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:20.960
<i>Okay.</i>

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:24.310
Oh, Mom might be worried about this, 
so could you check up on her for me?

00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:25.510
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:26.930
Okay, goodnight.

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:29.670
<i>Yeah, talk to you later. Night.</i>

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:37.550
<i>Maybe he's not going to call me today.</i>

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:47.660
Be a decent guy for once.

00:12:48.110 --> 00:12:51.240
You need to settle down already!

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:54.080
Thanks for always looking after him.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:57.040
I'm sorry for lying.

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:05.050
Koikimo

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:10.060
<b>Came to buy White Day Sweets</b>

00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:10.060
Koikimo

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:10.060
Maybe get her some
dacquoise or Florentines?

00:13:07.110 --> 00:13:10.060
Or go with
the classic
macarons...

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:10.060
Oh, they have
these, too...

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:12.220
Amakusa

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:12.640
Er, my bad, Ichika.

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:14.060
I forgot something.

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:15.280
One sec.

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:15.980
Sure.

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:19.850
Oh, hello.

00:13:19.850 --> 00:13:21.900
Oh... Hello.

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:25.320
It's nice to meet you. 
My name is Arima Ichika.

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:27.980
Rio-san and I are supposed 
to go shopping together.

00:13:28.900 --> 00:13:30.170
Ichika-san?

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:32.600
<i>So this is Ryo-san's...</i>

00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:37.970
So... has Ryo been bothering you?

00:13:37.970 --> 00:13:38.590
Huh?

00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:41.130
I heard that you two were acquainted.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:45.190
Oh, no. Ryo-san's been helping 
me figure out my career path...

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:48.220
and helping me out a lot in other ways, too.

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:49.470
He has?

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:50.350
Yes.

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:53.680
I think he's a good person.

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:56.430
I see.

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:57.860
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:00.310
Dad, she's...

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:01.910
We've already met.

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:04.120
If you'll excuse me.

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:09.720
He didn't say anything weird, did he?

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:11.360
Nope, everything's fine.

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:12.520
Good.

00:14:18.980 --> 00:14:22.830
But I don't wanna go flower 
viewing with <i>just</i> you!

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:24.290
<i>Well, I don't want this, either.</i>

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:27.740
This always happens when we're supposed 
to get together with our classmates.

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:30.000
Everyone makes other plans 
and it falls through.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.640
Man, it sucks being adults.

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:35.280
<i>Why doesn't anyone think about 
how I feel trying to host this thing?!</i>

00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:36.920
<i>You jerks!</i>

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:38.600
I guess we can just cancel, then.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:43.450
No way! I bought a tarp 
and got us some alcohol!

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:44.090
I even
bought snacks

00:14:43.450 --> 00:14:45.180
<i>Then I guess we'll have to invite people.</i>

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:46.480
Oh, I know!

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:48.860
<b>Arithmetic II</b>

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:48.860
You have a new message.

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:56.880
Say, Ichika. Want to go to a 
flower viewing this Sunday?

00:14:57.310 --> 00:14:59.210
Like looking at cherry blossoms? Yes!

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:03.540
Okay. Then let's meet up at 11:30.

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:04.250
Okay.

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:05.750
Masuda-san

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:05.750
One message sent

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:05.750
Sent

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:09.670
Oh, and it's going to be with 
my brother and Masuda-san.

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:10.440
Huh?

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:15.640
Man, I'm so happy it's sunny today.

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:18.180
The falling petals are a nice touch.

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:20.860
What do you two girls want to drink?

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:25.450
We have tea, fizzy drinks, and orange juice.

00:15:25.450 --> 00:15:26.780
I'll take some tea.

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:28.190
I'll take something fizzy.

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:31.760
You got it! Oh, feel free 
to use those cushions.

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:33.280
Thank you very much.

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:36.200
If you get cold, I've got 
blankets and hand warmers,

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:37.830
so just let me know.

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:40.340
You're so reliable, Masuda-san.

00:15:40.340 --> 00:15:41.740
I know, right?

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:44.280
I'm the one who got the 
stuff to keep us warm.

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:48.510
Don't tell them that, Ryo! I was 
trying to make myself look better!

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:49.860
Well, it's the truth.

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:51.590
Seriously...

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:51.590
<i>Maybe I'm just imagining it.</i>

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:55.400
<i>Ryo-san seems less excitable than usual.</i>

00:15:51.820 --> 00:15:55.400
You never plan these properly, anyway.

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:58.710
Ichika-san, would you like a blanket?

00:15:58.710 --> 00:16:01.180
Huh? Uh, yes.

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:03.520
Oh, right. Here.

00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:06.520
My mom made this for all of us.

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.520
Wow, that looks great.

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:10.720
Hey, that's awesome!

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:12.530
Yuriko-san's amazing, as always.

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:14.860
Here's a plate for you, Ryo-san.

00:16:14.860 --> 00:16:16.450
Oh, thank you very much.

00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:17.990
<b>Swoosh</b>

00:16:18.570 --> 00:16:21.200
Y-You're welcome.

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:25.420
Here's one for you, too, Masuda-san.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:26.670
Thanks.

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:31.380
Oh, yeah. My mom gave me something 
to give all of you, too.

00:16:28.150 --> 00:16:31.380
<b>Already eating</b>

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:38.700
Uh... So what is this?

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:41.890
It's
black...

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:40.130
I'm not sure.

00:16:40.130 --> 00:16:41.890
Oh, maybe...

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:42.890
<b>Grab</b>

00:16:43.340 --> 00:16:45.260
They're futomaki!

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:48.900
It's not Setsubun today, Mom.
At least cut them.

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:50.820
I'm digging in!

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:52.780
Hey, there's a note.

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:57.210
"One of these is loaded 
with wasabi. Love, Mom."

00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:01.020
Looks like you found the winner, Masuda-san.

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:03.940
Crap! Oh, God! My nose! My nasal cavities!

00:17:03.940 --> 00:17:05.960
Masuda-san, please drink some tea!

00:17:08.410 --> 00:17:09.380
Huh?

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:11.730
Damn. Looks like we're out of beer.

00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:13.000
I'll go buy some more.

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:16.130
I'll go with you. I want 
something from the food stalls.

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:20.750
Huh? Then I can just go... buy...

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:21.510
<b>Stare...</b>

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:21.510
m 0 0 l 40 0 l 40 170 l 0 170

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:21.510
Take-
the-
friggin'-
hint 
face

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:24.850
Oh, right! Yeah! Let's go, Rio-chan!

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:25.520
Huh?

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:27.470
We'll be back.

00:17:27.470 --> 00:17:29.030
Uh, wait, Rio!

00:17:29.030 --> 00:17:31.520
Watch over our area, guys!

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:33.690
<i>They were worried about us.</i>

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.680
Honestly, those two...

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:40.200
I think this is the first time we've been

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:42.990
alone like this since White Day.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:47.400
Has it been that long?

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:53.150
Oh, yeah. Ryo-san, I decided 
what school I wanted to go to.

00:17:53.150 --> 00:17:54.710
Oh, really?

00:17:55.020 --> 00:17:57.360
I found a school I really liked,

00:17:57.360 --> 00:18:00.650
and I can get my curator 
certification there, too.

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:03.260
I'm going to try to go there.

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:08.390
I see. I'm glad you found 
something you want to pursue.

00:18:09.070 --> 00:18:10.450
Thank you.

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:14.100
If there's anything I can help with, 
please don't hesitate to ask.

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:16.400
I might have to ask you to help me study.

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:19.010
Would you like me to make 
you another study guide?

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:21.260
For Ichika-san

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:21.260
<b>Mathematics Study Guide</b>

00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:21.490
I'll make it even better this time.

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:24.050
You don't have to do all that.

00:18:24.050 --> 00:18:27.880
Besides, I actually liked 
how homemade it looked.

00:18:29.230 --> 00:18:30.890
Then homemade it is.

00:18:30.890 --> 00:18:33.980
I'll make it look even 
more handmade this time.

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:36.190
What does that even mean?

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:43.460
I haven't had such a relaxed 
flower viewing in so long.

00:18:43.460 --> 00:18:44.740
Really?

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:48.020
My job has a flower viewing every year.

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:50.560
And with them, they all 
prefer their dumplings...

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:54.270
<b>Yay</b>

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:54.270
<b>Yay</b>

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:52.380
or rather, alcohol over their flowers.

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:54.270
Ah, I see.

00:18:54.580 --> 00:18:57.270
How long has it been since 
you went outside of work?

00:18:57.270 --> 00:19:03.550
Hmm... I think we went as a family 
when Rio was still in a stroller...

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:06.910
<b>The Best Candied Apples in Town</b>

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:06.910
<b>Straw-
berries</b>

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:06.910
<b>Apples</b>

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:06.910
<b>Mandarins</b>

00:19:03.550 --> 00:19:04.860
I think that was the last time.

00:19:04.860 --> 00:19:06.910
Huh? But that's so long ago.

00:19:07.130 --> 00:19:09.480
Oh, I remember now.

00:19:14.350 --> 00:19:18.230
If I remember correctly, 
it suddenly started raining,

00:19:18.230 --> 00:19:20.090
and we ended up leaving.

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:24.720
I was super depressed about that.

00:19:26.980 --> 00:19:32.100
But then my dad let me try a 
lottery draw on our way home.

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:32.100
<b>Lottery</b>

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:35.240
Oh, that's right. I won a toy.

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:37.610
I don't remember exactly what kind.

00:19:38.630 --> 00:19:39.770
How nostalgic.

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:45.120
That's right...

00:19:45.860 --> 00:19:49.210
We were still able to smile and talk back then.

00:19:53.780 --> 00:19:57.000
We don't get along very well.

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:02.300
My dad and my brother <i>really</i> don't get along.

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:05.160
They're like cats and dogs.

00:20:05.980 --> 00:20:10.280
<i>This is the first time Ryo-san's 
told me about their dad himself.</i>

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:14.110
Do you get along with 
your father, Ichika-san?

00:20:14.110 --> 00:20:18.730
Me? Hmm... I guess we're pretty close.

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:22.210
My father and I have been 
at odds for so long that

00:20:22.210 --> 00:20:24.500
we just don't know how to interact anymore.

00:20:25.340 --> 00:20:28.870
I saw him for the first time in a while 
the other day and talked to him,

00:20:29.310 --> 00:20:31.320
but we ended up in an argument.

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:37.620
I was able to tell him how I truly feel, sort of...

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:40.650
But I'm not sure if I got through to him.

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:45.920
I'm sorry. I must be boring you.

00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:48.380
No, I'm glad you told me all this.

00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:53.640
I wanted you to tell me something 
I didn't know about you...

00:20:54.470 --> 00:20:57.360
So I'm really glad you told me.

00:21:00.710 --> 00:21:03.370
How you truly feel...

00:21:06.730 --> 00:21:08.570
Ichika-san, there's a flower petal...

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:22.740
Ryo-san.

00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:27.340
Ryo-san, I think I...

00:21:30.870 --> 00:21:33.210
We bought some stuff!

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:36.700
Sorry, we ate some of it, though.

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:38.920
Look at these spiral-cut potatoes.

00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:42.340
O-Oh, wow! They look great!

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:44.750
Let's have some, Ryo-san.

00:21:44.750 --> 00:21:46.070
Oh, sure...

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:48.850
Wow, the sausages are spiral-cut, too.

00:21:48.850 --> 00:21:50.210
Aren't these great?

00:21:50.210 --> 00:21:52.330
We got yakisoba, too!

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:58.540
Man, we bought so much!

00:21:58.540 --> 00:22:00.330
You did.

00:22:00.870 --> 00:22:02.920
Hey, try the yakisoba, too!

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:04.040
Okay, okay...

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:40.250
Next Time

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:40.250
"You're Creepy"

00:23:36.090 --> 00:23:38.370
Next time, "You're Creepy."
